When and and or are used in the same expression, and has a higher precedence than or. This means the conditions joined with and are grouped together, as if they were inside parentheses. Precedence determines grouping, while short-circuiting determines whether the right operand needs to be evaluated:

Functions are reusable pieces of code that run when you call them. Python provides built-in functions, including print(), which you used in previous lessons.

Caesar cipher is an ecryption method that shifts letter in the alphabet to encode messages
A Caesar cipher encrypts text by replacing each letter of the plaintext with a letter a fixed number of positions later in the alphabet. For example, with a shift of 5, a would be replaced by f, b by g and so on.

